{"slug":"subarrays-with-k-different","title":"Subarrays With Exactly k Different Numbers","topic":"arrays-strings","difficulty":"hard","order":187,"tags":["arrays","sliding-window","counting"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Exactly k = at most k minus at most k-1","body":["Counting blocks with **exactly** `k` different values directly is awkward for a sliding window, because a window can stop being valid in two directions. Counting blocks with **at most** `k` different values is easy: it is valid as long as it has `<= k` different values, so shrink it from the left when it has too many.",{"code":"def at_most(k):\n    count = [0] * (n + 1); distinct = l = total = 0\n    for r in range(n):\n        if count[a[r]] == 0: distinct += 1\n        count[a[r]] += 1\n        while distinct > k:\n            count[a[l]] -= 1\n            if count[a[l]] == 0: distinct -= 1\n            l += 1\n        total += r - l + 1       # all blocks ending at r that start at l..r"},"Every block with exactly `k` different values has at most `k` and not at most `k - 1`. So the answer is `at_most(k) - at_most(k - 1)`. The trick of turning \"exactly\" into a difference of two \"at most\" counts is very common."]},"statement":["Given an array of `n` integers between 1 and `n` and a number `k`, count the blocks of consecutive elements that contain exactly `k` different values."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n` and `k`.","The second line has `n` integers between 1 and `n`."],"outputFormat":["Print the number of blocks."],"constraints":["1 <= k <= n <= 20000","1 <= each number <= n"],"examples":[{"input":"5 2\n1 2 1 2 3\n","output":"7\n","note":"The blocks with exactly two different values are [1 2], [2 1], [1 2], [2 3], [1 2 1], [2 1 2] and [1 2 1 2]: 7."}],"hints":["Counting \"at most k different\" with a window is easier than \"exactly k\".","For every right end r, all starts from the window start l to r give blocks with at most k different values.","The answer is `atMost(k) - atMost(k - 1)`."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nn, k = map(int, input().split())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n;\n    long long k;\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long k = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = Long.parseLong(next());\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["`atMost(k)` counts blocks with at most `k` different values using one sliding window. The blocks with exactly `k` are the difference between `atMost(k)` and `atMost(k - 1)`."],"complexity":"Time O(n), space O(n).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\ndef at_most(a, n, k):\n    count = [0] * (n + 1)\n    distinct = l = total = 0\n    for rr in range(n):\n        if count[a[rr]] == 0:\n            distinct += 1\n        count[a[rr]] += 1\n        while distinct > k:\n            count[a[l]] -= 1\n            if count[a[l]] == 0:\n                distinct -= 1\n            l += 1\n        total += rr - l + 1\n    return total\n\nn, k = map(int, input().split())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\nprint(at_most(a, n, k) - at_most(a, n, k - 1))\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long atMost(const vector<long long>& a, int n, long long k) {\n    vector<int> count(n + 1, 0);\n    long long distinct = 0, total = 0;\n    int l = 0;\n    for (int rr = 0; rr < n; rr++) {\n        if (count[a[rr]] == 0) distinct++;\n        count[a[rr]]++;\n        while (distinct > k) {\n            count[a[l]]--;\n            if (count[a[l]] == 0) distinct--;\n            l++;\n        }\n        total += rr - l + 1;\n    }\n    return total;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n;\n    long long k;\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    cout << atMost(a, n, k) - atMost(a, n, k - 1) << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    static long atMost(long[] a, int n, long k) {\n        int[] count = new int[n + 1];\n        long distinct = 0, total = 0;\n        int l = 0;\n        for (int rr = 0; rr < n; rr++) {\n            if (count[(int) a[rr]] == 0) distinct++;\n            count[(int) a[rr]]++;\n            while (distinct > k) {\n                count[(int) a[l]]--;\n                if (count[(int) a[l]] == 0) distinct--;\n                l++;\n            }\n            total += rr - l + 1;\n        }\n        return total;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long k = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = Long.parseLong(next());\n\n        System.out.println(atMost(a, (int) n, k) - atMost(a, (int) n, k - 1));\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"5 2\n1 2 1 2 3\n","output":"7\n"},{"input":"5 3\n1 2 1 3 4\n","output":"3\n"},{"input":"1 1\n1\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"4 1\n1 1 1 1\n","output":"10\n"},{"input":"4 4\n1 2 3 4\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"12 2\n2 3 2 3 1 2 1 4 2 1 1 4\n","output":"16\n"},{"input":"500 3\n2 6 3 8 5 2 4 1 1 3 7 5 5 4 6 2 2 5 8 8 8 6 7 4 2 3 3 8 3 8 1 2 2 1 4 3 4 8 1 4 1 8 4 7 5 7 4 2 4 7 8 7 2 4 8 6 4 3 8 1 3 4 5 2 3 8 6 7 4 1 3 4 3 8 6 7 4 2 6 1 6 1 2 7 4 1 3 1 8 8 8 3 3 8 6 6 5 4 1 4 5 7 8 8 5 7 7 2 1 8 8 4 4 1 1 2 8 1 4 4 6 4 5 6 6 1 4 6 6 2 6 6 4 6 6 8 3 4 1 3 5 8 6 7 7 6 4 2 8 7 5 3 4 8 3 4 7 5 3 6 1 2 1 8 1 8 1 5 1 3 4 3 5 4 6 4 3 2 2 6 8 4 3 5 7 6 3 4 2 1 1 4 2 2 8 1 4 5 5 4 1 7 7 5 6 5 2 8 6 4 8 6 7 1 1 5 8 7 5 5 8 6 5 5 7 1 1 5 3 7 8 8 4 5 3 6 2 7 5 8 1 3 6 7 3 5 2 6 5 4 6 2 4 5 7 1 3 1 1 2 4 1 1 6 6 5 8 1 6 2 3 6 4 5 5 2 2 6 1 2 3 2 4 6 1 5 5 7 2 4 6 7 1 3 2 5 6 2 5 5 6 1 1 1 6 1 3 2 5 4 1 1 4 3 4 4 4 7 3 7 1 4 1 7 2 4 6 7 5 7 5 3 1 3 3 4 3 6 6 8 5 6 6 8 7 5 6 1 7 8 3 5 5 5 2 8 1 4 4 4 2 5 1 7 4 3 6 1 6 7 7 6 8 5 4 5 1 2 1 7 2 6 8 7 6 2 1 6 1 6 5 8 8 4 2 8 6 5 2 5 3 5 8 7 8 6 4 6 6 3 2 3 5 6 1 1 1 4 8 7 8 7 1 2 3 4 4 1 2 8 7 7 2 8 8 3 1 8 4 6 6 5 4 2 2 6 7 3 2 7 3 8 4 1 1 6 6 3 3 5 2 5 8 4 1 1 7 8 7 8 3 8 7 6 5 5 4 2 2 5 3 4 6 1 1 3 6 8 7 2 8 6 6 7 2 6 6 7 8 5\n","output":"807\n"},{"input":"2000 5\n28 14 22 19 14 13 19 11 28 5 6 3 26 6 3 4 17 11 14 22 4 23 8 16 29 17 1 19 24 12 10 24 29 19 17 7 6 29 4 12 19 24 7 24 22 14 16 27 19 27 2 18 6 26 4 5 1 15 22 7 27 9 10 12 26 16 3 30 12 29 9 30 25 27 7 23 15 14 18 28 12 30 15 15 29 3 16 12 11 14 14 15 20 17 30 7 29 25 13 30 30 23 19 20 24 30 17 16 6 15 10 19 14 8 1 15 19 19 6 6 13 15 28 18 9 3 6 13 28 25 6 22 1 10 8 12 17 22 22 25 24 18 25 23 10 9 9 25 2 26 10 20 21 14 3 7 11 17 26 24 19 18 9 28 21 21 24